# ◈ packages.kde-qt.list — Qt5 / KDE Frameworks stack + partitioning tools
#
# RENAMED from packages.calamares.list — Calamares itself was dropped (kept
# hitting REQUIRED_USE/python-target churn and was ultimately not wanted for
# the ISO), but everything else in this list already builds cleanly on its
# own, so it stayed rather than being thrown out along with Calamares.
# Keeping the "kde-qt" name rather than "calamares" now that the actual
# installer isn't in here avoids the file being misleading later.
#
# CORRECTED AGAIN: this list originally requested dev-qt/qtcore, qtgui,
# qtwidgets, qtnetwork, qtdbus, qtquickcontrols2 as separate atoms — those
# are Qt5-style split module names, but everything actually in this list
# (kde-frameworks 6.x, kpmcore) needs Qt6, where Gentoo consolidates those
# five into dev-qt/qtbase itself via USE flags (confirmed against Gentoo's
# own Qt6 migration notes: qtcore→qtbase, qtgui→qtbase[gui],
# qtnetwork→qtbase[network], qtdbus→qtbase[dbus]; qtwidgets follows the
# same pattern). qtquickcontrols2 has no Qt6 equivalent package at all —
# "functionalities are still there but provided by different packages"
# per Gentoo's own notes — so it's dropped as an explicit atom; whatever
# still needs that functionality pulls in the real Qt6 package for it
# transitively. qtsvg, qtdeclarative, qtwayland, qttranslations stayed as
# separate atoms since those already built successfully standalone.
#
# If none of this ends up used for anything else either, it's a clean
# one-line removal per package the same way calamares was removed below —
# no need to keep dependencies around "just in case" once nothing needs them.

dev-qt/qtbase                     use:gui,widgets,network,dbus
dev-qt/qtsvg
dev-qt/qtdeclarative
dev-qt/qtwayland
dev-qt/qttranslations

kde-frameworks/extra-cmake-modules
kde-frameworks/kcoreaddons
kde-frameworks/kconfig
kde-frameworks/kconfigwidgets
kde-frameworks/kwidgetsaddons
kde-frameworks/kiconthemes
kde-frameworks/ki18n
kde-frameworks/solid
kde-frameworks/kservice
kde-frameworks/kpackage

sys-libs/kpmcore
sys-block/parted
sys-fs/lvm2
sys-fs/cryptsetup
sys-fs/e2fsprogs
sys-fs/dosfstools
sys-fs/ntfs3g

sys-auth/polkit
dev-cpp/yaml-cpp
dev-libs/boost
